# Long Albion /faction threads (Classic and Shrouded Isles, up to 1.65). New writing; place, class and
# specialization names are taken from docs/bot-voices/VERIFIED-NAMES.md and RESEARCH-BRIEF.md section 5.
# Mechanics are kept general wherever the period detail is not verified.

@kind debate
@realm alb

@topic cleric_specs
@levels 20-50
@scene alb_cleric_three_ways
@role B class=Cleric
@role C class=Armsman,Paladin,Mercenary
@role D type=Leveler
@role E type=NoLifer
@role F type=*
A: {q} respecced my cleric to smite last night and my guild acts like i kicked a dog | {q} went smite on my cleric and now nobody in guild will group me | {q} my guild found out i went smite and the reaction was not kind
B: smite cleric here, welcome to the club. we have jackets | smite is fine, ignore them. you can actually kill things now | as a fellow smite cleric, the looks never stop, you get used to it
C: as a tank i just want to know who is keeping me alive in a pull | the tank side of me wants to know who heals when you are busy smiting
A: i still heal. just not the biggest heals in the realm
D: half heals in a full group is how you wipe at the barrows | a half spec healer on a big pull is how the barrows eats you
B: or you just pull smaller. novel idea | so pull one at a time like grownups
~ 25
E: rejuv is the group spec, enhancement is the buff spec, smite is the solo spec. it is not complicated | three lines, three jobs. rejuv groups, enhancement buffs, smite solos
?C: enhancement buffs on a cleric make my day honestly | i will never say no to an enhancement cleric
A: and if i want to solo AND group?
E: then you pick one and suffer in the other | then you suffer a little everywhere, that is what a hybrid spec means
B: lol accurate
~ 30
F: sorry to jump in, how do clerics get the rez? is it a spec thing | quick newbie question, does every cleric get rez or only rejuv ones
B: every cleric rezzes, do not worry about that part | all of us rez, the spec only changes what else you do
F: ok cool ty, carry on arguing | ty! ok back to the fight, pretend i was never here
D: honest take, rejuv clerics get invites in seconds. smite clerics wait | real talk, a rejuv cleric shouting lfg gets eight tells. a smite cleric gets two
A: two is enough, i only need one good group
C: and i only need one cleric who watches my health bar | i am happy with any cleric that watches the health bars
~ 20
?E: the real crime is clerics who forget to rebuff after a death
B: guilty
D: we are all guilty of that one
A: ok, keeping smite for a month and then we see | fine, smite for a month, then i decide for real
C: need a cleric at the barrows right now actually, smite or not | speaking of which, we need a cleric at the barrows, any spec. pst
A: omw, smite and all | sending a tell, be nice to me

@topic friar_staff
@levels 15-50
@scene alb_friar_stick_or_heals
@role B class=Friar
@role C class=Friar,Cleric
@role D type=Socialite
@role E type=Daredevil
A: are friars healers that hit things or fighters that heal? | friar question, healer with a staff or fighter with heals? | so what is a friar actually for in a group
B: staff friar here. i am a fighter in a robe and proud of it | i spec staff. i am the robed brawler, the heals are a bonus
C: rejuv friar here, i am the healer and the staff is for decoration | i went rejuv and the staff mostly leans against a tree
B: decoration? my staff has more kills than your heals
C: and my heals have more saves than your staff
~ 25
D: are you two in the same guild? this sounds like a guild dinner | is this a family argument? it has that sound
B: same guild, same group, same argument every night | same group for a year. we have this fight weekly
?E: i grouped with a staff friar in cornwall once, he tanked a whole bear pull | there was a staff friar in my cornwall group who held three bears off the cleric
B: see, legends spread
C: one bear pull does not make a legend
A: what about enhancement? never see anyone talk about that | nobody ever mentions enhancement friars, are they a thing?
C: enhancement friars buff the whole group, quietly the best of us | the buffs from an enhancement friar are no joke, they just make no noise
B: quiet is the word. i like being heard | quiet is right. i prefer being loud with a stick
~ 30
E: honest question, can a staff friar solo the 30s? | can a stick friar actually solo once the cons get tough
B: slowly, with lots of sitting, but yes | yes, if you like long sits between pulls
?C: and lots of running away
B: strategic walking
D: strategic walking, i am stealing that | adding strategic walking to my vocabulary
~ 20
A: so the answer is staff for fun, rejuv for groups, enhancement for being loved quietly | ok summary: staff for fun, rejuv for invites, enhancement for quiet glory
C: that is fair | i can live with that summary
B: staff for glory you mean | you misspelled staff for glory
?E: can we get a friar statue in camelot already
D: a friar statue holding a staff and a heal potion | holding a staff in one hand and a bandage in the other

@topic armsman_weapons
@levels 25-50
@scene alb_armsman_three_weapons
@role B class=Armsman
@role C class=Armsman
@role D type=NoLifer
@role E class=Cleric,Friar
A: armsmen, settle something for me. polearm, two hander or crossbow? | {q} new armsman, which weapon line actually matters | polearm or two handed, and is crossbow worth any points at all
B: polearm. the reach, the positional styles, it feels like what an armsman should be | polearm all day, nothing says albion like a halberd
C: two handed. bigger swings, simpler setup, less fussing with positions | two hander here. i do not want to dance around a monster to hit hard
B: the dancing is the fun part | positionals are half the class, you skip half the class
C: the dancing gets you killed when the healer runs out of power
~ 25
D: nobody is mentioning shields and parry. a tanking armsman needs them | what about a shield build? in the barrows the sword and board armsman is king
B: shield is for the group tank, i get that. but the damage is what gets you invites
D: the damage gets you aggro you cannot keep | a damage armsman just means the healer works twice as hard
?E: as the healer i have opinions, but i will keep them to myself | healer here, i will just say i prefer the one with a shield
A: and the crossbow? i see some armsmen pulling with one
C: a few points for pulling, nothing more | a pull tool, not a weapon. dont sink much into it
B: some guys swear by it in the frontier to tag runners
~ 30
?A: what do you two use in the frontier then
C: two hander, i want to drop a caster fast | two handed in rvr, casters fold quickly
B: polearm, and i stand at the door like a gate
D: that is the most armsman sentence ever written | polearm armsman at a door is the most albion picture there is
E: and i heal both of you either way | either way it is me keeping you upright
~ 20
A: still cannot decide honestly | i think i am more confused than when i asked
B: polearm. trust me | go polearm, you will thank me at level 40
C: two hander. trust me instead
D: that is what a respec is for, try both | spec one, and if you hate it, respec. not the end of the world
A: ...i will think about it while i level | ok i will just flip a coin at the trainer

@topic paladin_chants
@levels 20-50
@scene alb_paladin_twisting
@role B class=Paladin
@role C class=Minstrel
@role D type=Leveler
@role E type=Socialite
A: paladins, how many chants do you actually keep going at once | {q} how do paladins juggle chants without going crazy | is chant twisting on a paladin worth learning or just a show off thing
B: one steady, and i twist more in between swings | depends on the fight. endurance always, then i weave in the heal and the damage
C: minstrel here, welcome to the twisting club, we have headaches | twisting is a full time job, ask any minstrel
D: i have grouped with paladins who twist and ones who dont. night and day difference
A: what makes it so hard?
B: timing. you lose a beat and the whole group feels it | one late key press and the endurance drops right when the tank needs it
?C: and someone always asks why their run speed stopped | and then everyone yells at you in group chat
~ 25
E: i just like having a paladin around, the group feels sturdier | groups with a paladin feel calmer to me, cant explain it
B: that is the chants doing their job. nobody notices till they stop
D: brb, pull coming, keep arguing without me | gtg pull, this is a good one though, save it for me
C: so paladin damage, is it really as low as people say
